primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1699469751", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "161896287", "author": {"steamid": "76561198095106900", "personaname": "Atom", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198095106900/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 16, "playtime_forever": 5563, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 5563, "last_played": 1708738805, "avatar": "b8d68f3a3f24a0e8efe626a9b6dccb20c03c98d4"}, "language": "english", "review": "I purposefully waited to leave a review for this game because, even though I thoroughly enjoyed it and have every achievement, I haven't felt any strong desire to go back and play it since then.\n\nI have every achievement in Risk of Rain 1 and 2 and I am constantly replaying the second one with friends or aiming for higher eclipse levels. I only really went back to play the first one before this game came out for the nostalgia. But this game sadly fell off my radar once I was done doing everything.\n\nIn hindsight, that feels like a really silly thing to say. \"Once I did everything the game has to offer I got kinda bored of it\". I really enjoyed playing this game and doing everything, but the reason I play rogue-likes is for the replay-ability. I am constantly revisiting Slay the Spire, FTL, RoR2, etc even though I've done everything. I can't pinpoint the exact reason, but I just haven't come back to this one.\n\nAll that to say, I still recommend this if you're looking for a challenging rogue-like experience.", "timestamp_created": 1711905681, "timestamp_updated": 1711905681, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1699469751", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "161860306", "author": {"steamid": "76561198136397423", "personanam